I'm a Senior Principal Applied Scientist in the Automated Reasoning Group at [AWS](https://aws.amazon.com/).
I'm also the Chief Architect and co-founder of the [Lean FRO](https://lean-fro.org),
a non-profit organization dedicated to the development of the [Lean](https://lean-lang.org) theorem prover and programming language.

My research areas are automated reasoning, theorem proving, decision procedures, SAT and SMT. I am the main architect of [Lean](https://lean-lang.org) and [Z3](https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3). Recipient of the Herbrand and CAV awards, and the ACM SIGPLAN Software Award for both Z3 and Lean.

# Current Work

- [Lean Theorem Prover and Programming Language](https://lean-lang.org) — expressive types, powerful automation, a programmable ecosystem
- [grind](https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/The--grind--tactic/) — a Lean tactic inspired by modern SMT solvers, combining E-matching, congruence closure, and linear arithmetic
- [sym](/notes/2026-3-13-sym---interactive-mode-for-scalable-verification/) — a new framework for building scalable software and hardware verification tools in Lean

